      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "> This leads to confusion when test results from different builds are aggregated together,\n\nWhat build results are aggregated together and why? CDash displays test deltas (-1, +1) based on the previous build with the same build name and site name.\n\nWe should make sure that `ENABLE_WALLET`, `ENABLE_IPC` and `BUILD_GUI_TESTS` should remain consistent. Don't submit test results with different values of `ENABLE_WALLET` and identical build name. A naming convention for build names that encodes those settings helps. You seem to already do that with build names like \"Alpine, depends, no GUI\".",
      "user": {
        "login": "purpleKarrot",
        "id": 185240,
        "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE4NTI0MA==",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/185240?v=4",
